      <div id="help-tutorial-grid" class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-2.5 text-[11.5px] leading-relaxed">

        <!-- CARD 1: Disable State (Dis R24) & Polarity Invert (R16/17/18[4]) -->
        <article data-help-group="dis_inv" class="lg:col-span-2 bg-lab-card border border-cyan-500/35 rounded-lg p-3 space-y-2.5">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-bold text-cyan-300">1. Disable State (<code class="font-mono text-amber-300">Dis R24[1:0] / [3:2] / [5:4]</code>) &amp; Polarity Invert (<code class="font-mono text-amber-300">R16/17/18[4]</code>)</h3>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-slate-400">Reg 24 (0x18) · Reg 3 (OEB) · Reg 16–18</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-slate-300">
            <strong>Disable State (<code class="font-mono text-cyan-300">Dis</code>)</strong> controls what electrical state each clock pin (<code class="font-mono">CLK0=R24[1:0]</code>, <code class="font-mono">CLK1=R24[3:2]</code>, <code class="font-mono">CLK2=R24[5:4]</code>) holds whenever the output is disabled via <code class="font-mono">Reg 3</code> (Output Enable Mask <code class="font-mono">OEB</code>) or the hardware <code class="font-mono">OEB</code> pin. Try switching CH2 (or CH0) to <strong>Off / Disabled</strong> and changing <code class="font-mono">Dis</code> to watch its dashed line move on the oscilloscope:
          </p>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-4 gap-2">
            <div class="bg-lab-bg border border-lab-border rounded p-2 space-y-1">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between font-mono text-[11px]">
                <span class="font-bold text-white">Low (0V)</span>
                <span class="text-cyan-400">00b</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-300">Actively pulls the pin to <strong>GND (0V)</strong> when disabled. Best general-purpose default for digital clock inputs and RF mixers so the trace never floats or picks up stray noise.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-lab-bg border border-lab-border rounded p-2 space-y-1">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between font-mono text-[11px]">
                <span class="font-bold text-white">High (3.3V)</span>
                <span class="text-cyan-400">01b</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-300">Actively drives the pin to <strong>VDD (3.3V)</strong> when disabled. Use for active-low logic, pull-up-style resting states, or downstream gates that expect a logic-1 idle level.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-lab-bg border border-lab-border rounded p-2 space-y-1">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between font-mono text-[11px]">
                <span class="font-bold text-white">High-Z</span>
                <span class="text-cyan-400">10b</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-300"><strong>Tri-states (disconnects)</strong> the output buffer so the pin floats at high impedance. Use when sharing a clock bus with another oscillator, reducing load capacitance, or avoiding DC current into 50 &Omega; loads.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-lab-bg border border-amber-500/35 rounded p-2 space-y-1">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between font-mono text-[11px]">
                <span class="font-bold text-amber-300">Never (PDN=1)</span>
                <span class="text-amber-400">11b</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-300">Tells hardware to <strong>ignore <code class="font-mono">Reg 3</code> (OEB)</strong> so the output stays permanently enabled during OEB blanking (e.g., an MCU main clock). <em>Note: Setting Mode = Off in this tool still sets <code class="font-mono">CLKx_PDN=1</code> (<code class="font-mono">Reg 16+i[7]</code>), which powers down the driver completely.</em></p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-lab-bg/80 border border-lab-border rounded p-2 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-2">
            <div>
              <span class="font-bold text-rose-300 font-mono">Normal 0° / INV 180° (Reg 16/17/18 [bit 4], CLKx_INV):</span>
              <span class="text-slate-300"> Hardware-inverts the output waveform by an exact <strong>180°</strong> inside the output buffer with zero PLL phase error. Essential for push-pull drivers, balanced RF mixers, and 180° differential clock pairs. Switch the scope to <strong>Trig</strong> to watch the rising edge flip immediately to a falling edge.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- CARD 2: Operating Modes -->
        <article data-help-group="modes" class="bg-lab-card border border-lab-border rounded-lg p-3 space-y-2">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-bold text-cyan-300">2. Channel Operating Modes (All 8 Modes)</h3>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-slate-400">Reg 3 · Reg 16–18 · Reg 165–167</span>
          </div>
          <ul class="space-y-1 text-[11px] text-slate-300">
            <li><strong class="text-white">Off / Disabled:</strong> Sets <code class="font-mono text-amber-300">Reg 3</code> (<code class="font-mono">OEB=1</code>) and <code class="font-mono text-amber-300">Reg 16+i[7]=1</code> (<code class="font-mono">PDN</code>). Pin rests at the state chosen in <code class="font-mono">Dis R24</code>.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Fractional MultiSynth:</strong> Default mode. Uses fractional divider <code class="font-mono">a + b/c</code> (<code class="font-mono">8..1800</code>) to generate virtually any frequency to sub-Hz precision.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Integer Low-Jitter Mode:</strong> Locks an even-integer MultiSynth (<code class="font-mono text-amber-300">MSx_INT=1</code>, <code class="font-mono">Reg 16+i[6]</code>) for minimal spurs and lowest phase noise (best for VFOs/MCU clocks).</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Quadrature I/Q 90° (CLK0+1):</strong> Couples CH0 &amp; CH1 on PLLA at equal frequency and writes <code class="font-mono text-amber-300">Reg 166</code> (<code class="font-mono">CLK1_PHOFF</code>) for an exact 90° SDR quadrature local oscillator.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Custom Phase Offset (0°–360°):</strong> Unlocks the <code class="font-mono">Phase</code> slider to delay the channel in <code class="font-mono">T_VCO / 4</code> steps via <code class="font-mono text-amber-300">Reg 165–167</code> (applied on <code class="font-mono">Reg 177</code> PLL soft-reset).</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Differential Pair (180° Inv):</strong> Couples CH0 &amp; CH1 at equal frequency on PLLA and forces <code class="font-mono text-amber-300">Reg 17[4]</code> (<code class="font-mono">CLK1_INV=1</code>) for complementary differential clocks.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Spread Spectrum (PLLA EMI):</strong> Enables <code class="font-mono text-amber-300">Reg 149–161</code> (<code class="font-mono">SSC_EN=1</code>) on PLLA to dither frequency by <code class="font-mono">0.1%–2.5%</code> (Down-spread or Center-spread via <code class="font-mono">Reg 151[7]</code>) and cut EMI peaks.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Direct XTAL Bypass:</strong> Routes the crystal straight to the output buffer (<code class="font-mono text-amber-300">CLKx_SRC=00</code>), bypassing PLL &amp; MultiSynth. Requires <code class="font-mono">XO Fanout</code> (<code class="font-mono">Reg 187[6]=1</code>).</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <!-- CARD 3: Frequency Tuning & PLL Select -->
        <article data-help-group="modes" class="bg-lab-card border border-lab-border rounded-lg p-3 space-y-2">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-bold text-cyan-300">3. Frequency Tuning Controls &amp; PLL Select</h3>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-slate-400">Reg 42–65 (MS0–2) · Reg 16–18[5]</span>
          </div>
          <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-[11px] text-slate-300">
            <li><strong class="text-white">PLL Select (<code class="font-mono text-amber-300">PLLA / PLLB</code>, <code class="font-mono">Reg 16+i[5]</code>):</strong> Chooses which 600–900 MHz VCO drives MultiSynth <code class="font-mono">MSx</code>. Use separate PLLs for independent frequencies, or share one PLL when phase-locking two outputs.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Quick Presets (<code class="font-mono">8k</code> .. <code class="font-mono">145M</code>) &amp; Direct Hz Input:</strong> Jump straight to common RF/IF bands or type any exact frequency from <code class="font-mono">1,000 Hz</code> to <code class="font-mono">225,000,000 Hz</code>. Above <code class="font-mono">150 MHz</code>, the Si5351A automatically enters <code class="font-mono">DIVBY4</code> mode (<code class="font-mono">MS=÷4</code>).</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Band Sweep (Log Slider) &amp; Step (<code class="font-mono">10</code> .. <code class="font-mono">1M</code>):</strong> Smoothly sweeps <code class="font-mono">8 kHz – 160 MHz</code> logarithmically; Step buttons set the increment used by the <code class="font-mono">-</code> / <code class="font-mono">+</code> nudge buttons.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Fine Trim (<code class="font-mono">&plusmn;50 kHz</code>, 10 Hz step):</strong> Works like a radio VFO clarifier/RIT, adding an offset to <code class="font-mono">baseHz</code>. At <code class="font-mono">14.2 MHz</code>, <code class="font-mono">&plusmn;50 kHz</code> is a fine <code class="font-mono">&plusmn;0.35%</code> shift; at <code class="font-mono">100 kHz</code>, it sweeps a full <code class="font-mono">3&times;</code> (<code class="font-mono">50–150 kHz</code>) across the scope.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Output Readout Box:</strong> Shows the <em>actual</em> hardware frequency after rational approximation, exact error in <code class="font-mono">Hz / ppb</code>, divider parameters (<code class="font-mono">MSx</code> &amp; <code class="font-mono">R</code>), live register hex bytes, and hardware limit warnings.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <!-- CARD 4: Phase, Drive & R-Div -->
        <article data-help-group="sliders" class="bg-lab-card border border-lab-border rounded-lg p-3 space-y-2">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-bold text-amber-300">4. Phase, Drive Strength &amp; R-Div Sliders</h3>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-slate-400">Reg 165–167 · Reg 16–18[1:0] · Reg 44/52/60[6:4]</span>
          </div>
          <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-[11px] text-slate-300">
            <li><strong class="text-white">Phase (<code class="font-mono text-amber-300">Reg 165/166/167</code>, <code class="font-mono">CLKx_PHOFF[6:0]</code>):</strong> Sets initial phase delay in <code class="font-mono">T_VCO / 4</code> increments (<code class="font-mono">0..127</code>). Because the register is 7-bit (max 127), very low frequencies with huge dividers clamp at 127 steps. Always requires a PLL Soft Reset (<code class="font-mono">Reg 177</code>) to latch.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Drive (<code class="font-mono text-amber-300">Reg 16/17/18[1:0]</code>, <code class="font-mono">CLKx_IDRV</code>):</strong> Output buffer current:
              <code class="font-mono">2mA (00)</code> = lowest power &amp; softest harmonics;
              <code class="font-mono">4mA (01)</code> = standard PCB logic;
              <code class="font-mono">6mA (10)</code> = capacitive/coax loads;
              <code class="font-mono">8mA (11)</code> = max swing (~10 dBm into 50 &Omega;) &amp; fastest edges. Visible directly as vertical wave height on the scope!
            </li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">R-Div (<code class="font-mono text-amber-300">Reg 44/52/60[6:4]</code>, <code class="font-mono">Rx_DIV[2:0]</code>):</strong> Post-MultiSynth power-of-2 divider (<code class="font-mono">Auto</code>, <code class="font-mono">/1</code> to <code class="font-mono">/128</code>). Required below <code class="font-mono">500 kHz</code> because MultiSynth max divider is <code class="font-mono">1800</code> (fractional) / <code class="font-mono">2048</code> (integer)—so in <code class="font-mono">Integer</code> mode <code class="font-mono">Auto</code> keeps <code class="font-mono">/1</code> down to <code class="font-mono">≈293 kHz</code> (<code class="font-mono">600 MHz ÷ 2048</code>). Leave on <code class="font-mono">Auto</code> unless testing hardware limits—forcing too high an R-Div at MHz hits the 900 MHz VCO cap, while forcing <code class="font-mono">/1</code> at 8 kHz clamps at <code class="font-mono">MS=÷1800</code>.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <!-- CARD 5: Global XTAL, Calib Trim, Fanout & PLL Cards -->
        <article data-help-group="global" class="bg-lab-card border border-lab-border rounded-lg p-3 space-y-2">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-bold text-emerald-300">5. Global XTAL, Calib Trim, Fanout &amp; PLL Telemetry</h3>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-slate-400">Reg 183 · Reg 187 · Reg 26–41</span>
          </div>
          <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-[11px] text-slate-300">
            <li><strong class="text-white">XTAL &amp; Load Cap (<code class="font-mono text-amber-300">Reg 183 / 0xB7</code>):</strong> Sets your board's crystal (<code class="font-mono">25 MHz</code> on CJMCU-5351, <code class="font-mono">27 MHz</code>, or custom <code class="font-mono">10–40 MHz</code>) and connects internal <code class="font-mono">6pF / 8pF / 10pF</code> load capacitors (<code class="font-mono">XTAL_CL[7:6]</code>) across XA/XB with no external caps needed.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Calib Trim (<code class="font-mono">&plusmn;500 ppm</code>):</strong> Software crystal calibration (<code class="font-mono">f_eff = f_xtal &times; (1 + ppm/10⁶)</code>). Measure a known output (e.g. 10 MHz) on a counter and dial in the ppm offset so all 3 channels synthesize true frequency.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Fanout (<code class="font-mono text-amber-300">Reg 187 / 0xBB</code>):</strong> <code class="font-mono">XO [b6]</code> routes XTAL directly to outputs (needed for Bypass); <code class="font-mono">MS0/4 [b4]</code> allows sharing MultiSynth 0/4 across clocks; <code class="font-mono">CLKIN [b7]</code> is Si5351C-only (keep OFF on Si5351A).</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">PLLA &amp; PLLB Telemetry Cards (<code class="font-mono">Reg 26–41</code>):</strong> Live VCO frequency (datasheet spec <code class="font-mono">600–900 MHz</code>, shown as <code class="font-mono text-emerald-400">IN SPEC</code>), multiplier ratio (<code class="font-mono">Int</code> vs fractional), active channel users, and <code class="font-mono text-rose-300">SS</code> Spread Spectrum indicator.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <!-- CARD 6: Oscilloscope, Presets & Workspace Tabs -->
        <article data-help-group="scope" class="lg:col-span-2 bg-lab-card border border-lab-border rounded-lg p-3 space-y-2">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-bold text-purple-300">6. Live Oscilloscope, System Presets &amp; Workspace Tabs</h3>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-slate-400">True Timebase · Signal Routing · C Export</span>
          </div>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-2.5 text-[11px] text-slate-300">
            <ul class="space-y-1">
              <li><strong class="text-white">Time/Div (<code class="font-mono">Auto (Real)</code>, <code class="font-mono">1 ns/div</code>–<code class="font-mono">100 µs/div</code>, <code class="font-mono">Log</code>):</strong> Real shared 10-division horizontal timebase showing exact frequency ratios. Fast channels (e.g. <code class="font-mono">160 MHz</code> beside <code class="font-mono">38 kHz</code>) render as a peak-detect <strong>HF BAND</strong> until you zoom Time/Div down to <code class="font-mono">2 ns/div</code>.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-white">Free / Trig &amp; Pause:</strong> <code class="font-mono">Free</code> runs continuously like a live scope; <code class="font-mono">Trig</code> locks a rising edge at Division 1 (<code class="font-mono text-emerald-400">T</code>) so you can inspect exact pulse widths, <code class="font-mono">90°</code> I/Q shifts, and <code class="font-mono">INV 180°</code> flips. <code class="font-mono">Pause</code> freezes the display.</li>
            </ul>
            <ul class="space-y-1">
              <li><strong class="text-white">Top Presets (<code class="font-mono">HF VFO+BFO</code>, <code class="font-mono">I/Q 90°</code>, <code class="font-mono">2m VHF+IF</code>, <code class="font-mono">Diff 180°</code>, <code class="font-mono">SpreadSpec</code>):</strong> One-click real-world RF &amp; digital clock configurations to explore how PLLs, MultiSynth dividers, phase offsets, and inversion work together.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-white">5 Bottom Tabs:</strong> <strong>Signal Routing</strong> (live block diagram), <strong>Register Map</strong> (hex/binary <code class="font-mono">Reg 0–187</code>), <strong>C Code Export</strong> (ready-to-compile <code class="font-mono">CH32V003 / Arduino / STM32 / Raw</code> headers), <strong>Datasheet &amp; Regs</strong> (AN619 formulas + live values), and <strong>Embeetle + WCH</strong> (wiring &amp; flashing guide).</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- CARD 7: Complete Si5351A Register Bitfields & Live Register Map -->
        <article data-help-group="regs" class="lg:col-span-2 bg-lab-card border border-amber-500/35 rounded-lg p-3 space-y-3">
